{"paper_id": "paper-467615f7deaa4d73", "doi": "10.1186/s12879-026-14066-z", "title": "Epidemiological characteristics of severe fever with thrombocytopenia syndrome (SFTS) in China, 2010–2024: a fifteen-year national surveillance analysis", "analysis": {"analysis": {"research_question_and_background": "This study was needed to characterize the evolving epidemiological patterns of severe fever with thrombocytopenia syndrome (SFTS) in China, as its incidence has risen steadily since 2009 with expanding geographic scope.", "study_design_and_population": "This retrospective descriptive study included clinically diagnosed and laboratory-confirmed SFTS cases from the China Information System for Disease Control and Prevention (CISDCP) between 2010 and 2024.", "methods": "Joinpoint regression was used to analyze incidence trends, and case fatality rate (CFR) differences were assessed by chi-squared or Fisher’s exact tests, with temporal trends evaluated by linear regression.", "main_results": "During 2010–2024, 30 provinces reported 34,055 cases, with an incidence rate showing a fluctuating upward trend (AAPC: 43.28%; 95% CI: 43.23%–43.33%; P < 0.01). The average CFR was 4.79%, increasing with age to 9.15% among those aged 85 years and above.", "interpretation_and_novelty": "The authors interpreted the findings as indicating a marked increase in reported incidence and considerable geographical expansion of SFTS, with the rapid rise in cases in provinces like Anhui suggesting a need to reevaluate ecological and social transmission factors.", "scientific_and_public_health_significance": "The findings inform surveillance priorities by highlighting the need to monitor geographic expansion and elderly mortality risk, and to reevaluate ecological and social factors driving transmission in newly affected areas.", "limitations_and_evidence_strength": "The evidence strength is moderate due to the retrospective descriptive design and reliance on surveillance data, which may have limitations in case ascertainment and reporting completeness."}, "summary_en": "This fifteen-year national surveillance analysis of severe fever with thrombocytopenia syndrome (SFTS) in China (2010–2024) reveals a significant increase in incidence and geographic expansion. Over 34,000 cases were reported across 30 provinces, with an average annual percent change of 43.28%. The case fatality rate was 4.79%, rising to 9.15% in those aged 85 and above. While the overall CFR showed a declining trend, mortality in elderly subgroups remains a concern. The rapid rise in cases in provinces like Anhui indicates a need to reassess ecological and social transmission factors. The study underscores the importance of enhanced surveillance and targeted interventions for high-risk populations.", "evidence_ids": {"research_question_and_background": ["F1"], "study_design_and_population": ["F3"], "methods": ["F4", "F5"], "main_results": ["F6", "F7", "F10"], "interpretation_and_novelty": ["F11", "F12"], "scientific_and_public_health_significance": ["F12", "F13"], "limitations_and_evidence_strength": ["F17", "F18"]}, "confidence": "low", "postprocess_audit": {"removed_duplicate_sentences": 0, "repaired_incomplete_fields": [], "evidence_replacements": [], "policy": "v10-exclusive-rhetorical-fields-1"}, "language_contract": {"policy_version": "v17.1-source-language-safe-english-1", "source_language": "en", "verified_english": true, "replacements": [], "original_evidence_preserved": false}, "status": "passed", "kind": "research", "provider": "bigmodel", "model": "glm-4.5-air", "attempts": [{"task": "paper_research_analysis", "provider": "gemini", "model": "", "at": "2026-07-29T20:49:59+00:00", "status": "skipped", "failure_category": "authentication_failed", "error": "authentication_failed"}, {"task": "paper_research_analysis", "provider": "bigmodel", "model": "glm-4.5", "at": "2026-07-29T20:49:59+00:00", "status": "skipped", "failure_category": "model_cooldown", "error": "model is temporaril