{"paper_id": "paper-c612bd298e1bbdaf", "doi": "10.1016/j.nmni.2026.101819", "title": "Macrogenomic analysis showcases the diversity of tick RNA viruses in Mentougou, Beijing, China", "analysis": {"analysis": {"research_question_and_background": "The study aimed to address the lack of characterization of tick-borne virus diversity in Beijing, highlighting the importance of understanding these viruses given their potential impact on human health.", "study_design_and_population": "The study was conducted in Mentougou District, Beijing, from 2023 to 2024, using tick samples collected from this region to investigate the diversity of tick RNA viruses.", "methods": "Metagenomic sequencing was performed on tick samples, followed by quality control, de novo assembly, and viral sequence identification. Phylogenetic and evolutionary analyses were conducted to classify the viruses.", "main_results": "The study identified 19 distinct viral species across 12 families, including six novel viruses from five virus families, with one potential pathogen, Tick jingmen-like virus, detected in the selected pathogens.", "interpretation_and_novelty": "The authors interpreted these findings as evidence of previously unrecognized diversity of tick-borne viruses in Mentougou District, emphasizing the novelty of discovering six new viral species.", "scientific_and_public_health_significance": "These findings provide essential baseline data for future surveillance strategies and prevention efforts of tick-borne diseases in the Beijing metropolitan area.", "limitations_and_evidence_strength": "The study is limited by its focus on a single geographic location, and the evidence is moderate due to the absence of comparative data with other regions or species."}, "summary_en": "This study conducted a macrogenomic analysis of tick samples from Mentougou District, Beijing, to explore the diversity of tick RNA viruses. The research identified 19 distinct viral species across 12 families, including six 